01:57:17,680 --> 01:57:19,680
So what's going to happen?

297
01:57:19,680 --> 01:57:20,180
All right.

298
01:57:20,180 --> 01:57:24,180
So this is going to be one defection leads to the permanent inclusion.

299
01:57:24,180 --> 01:57:30,180
So collusion is going to be sustainable as long as a 1 over n share of the monopoly profits

300
01:57:30,180 --> 01:57:35,180
is valued more than 100% of the monopoly profits once followed by 0 plus forever.

301
01:57:35,180 --> 01:57:37,180
And if we write this down, it says, well, look.

302
01:57:37,180 --> 01:57:38,180
All right.

303
01:57:38,180 --> 01:57:48,180
So we can either have 1 over n from time t equals 0 to infinity of the discounted sum of the monopoly profits.

304
01:57:48,180 --> 01:57:50,180
So that's what you get from colluding.

305
01:57:50,180 --> 01:57:53,180
Remember, that is your personal discount factor,

306
01:57:53,180 --> 01:57:58,180
although it could be based upon market interest rates or it could be based upon individual patience.

307
01:57:58,180 --> 01:58:04,180
So if you collude, then you get 1 n of the monopoly profits forever.

308
01:58:04,180 --> 01:58:10,180
On the other hand, if you defect, then you get all the monopoly profits once.

309
01:58:10,180 --> 01:58:12,180
How do you do that?

310
01:58:12,180 --> 01:58:14,180
Well, all the other firms are charging monopoly profits.

311
01:58:14,180 --> 01:58:17,180
And what do you do to steal it from them and steal it all from them?

312
01:58:17,180 --> 01:58:19,180
You charge how much less?

313
01:58:19,180 --> 01:58:21,180
Monopoly profits minus epsilon.

314
01:58:21,180 --> 01:58:22,180
Yes, exactly.

315
01:58:22,180 --> 01:58:25,180
And that will steal the entire market for you.

316
01:58:25,180 --> 01:58:31,180
And again, if it's truly infinitesimal, then actually mathematically it is to exactly equal the monopoly profits.

317
01:58:31,180 --> 01:58:33,180
It's just rounding here.

318
01:58:33,180 --> 01:58:35,180
So you get all the monopoly profits for one turn.

319
01:58:35,180 --> 01:58:44,180
And then if we have a blank trigger strategy, so one episode of collusion ends collusion forever,

320
01:58:44,180 --> 01:58:48,180
then what do recurring firms earn forever more after that?

321
01:58:48,180 --> 01:58:50,180
No profits at all.

322
01:58:50,180 --> 01:58:55,180
So it's a pretty easy equation to solve, pretty easy inequality to solve.

323
01:58:55,180 --> 01:58:59,180
So you can either have all the monopoly profits once for breaking the collusion,

324
01:58:59,180 --> 01:59:02,180
or you can have a 1 over n share forever.

325
01:59:02,180 --> 01:59:07,180
And if you just do the math, wow, we can even divide through by that pi m,

326
01:59:07,180 --> 01:59:17,180
and then we get the result that cooperation is sustainable as long as n over 1 minus n is less than or equal to beta.

